> Chelsea Handler Makes[ Her Next Move]...And It's a Big One!
Don't worry, the[ funny] lady will still[ be] around to make us laugh.
Earlier this year, Chelsea Handler announced that Chelsea Lately would come to an end[—]and I, for one, was super bummed, because[ Handler] has[ been the lone female] voice in late night talk shows for, well, ever[,] basically. As much as I love Jimmy Fallon, Seth Meyers and Stephen Colbert, post-11:30 p.m. TV would be a lot...quieter[ (]and tamer) without Handler.
To[ my] relief, Handler just announced[ her next move,] and it['s] a big one[—the comed]ienne is[ headed to] Netflix[,] where she'll launch an[ on-]demand new talk show in 2016. Obviously, that's not nearly soon enough[,] so, to tide us over, she's airing a stand-[up] special based on her latest book, “Uganda Be Kidding Me,”[ on] October 16, and a series of docu-specials, tacking topics from NASCAR and politics to the NBA draft and Silicon Valley, throughout 2015. I mean, who does't want to hear Handler riff on Nascar?
It should be super interesting to see how Handler's new show fares[ on] a network that's made it's name on binge-watching (try to tell me you didn't watch all of Orange Is The New[ Black] or House of[ Cards in] one[ go,] I dare you). Obviously,[ the] talk shows as we know them are meant to be watched nightly[,] as a reaction to the news of the day. Will people start[ tuning in] to[ Netflix] as if[ it] was just another channel, or will people end up watching old news[ on] demand? Late[ night TV] has already seen a ton of shake-ups this year (see: Fallon, Meyers and Colbert), but[,] if anyone could[ take a step further],[ my money]'s on Handler.

